# REQUIRES: python-api, parmed
# The products of force matching with the extra points of Amber
# (D384, #771), on the CPU: OPC from a prmtop, cut by ParmEd,
# the product in theta against a NumPy Phi, and the derivative in the
# positions with the curvature of the placement (D387),
# its part of the extra points against a NumPy Phi and the whole against
# differences of Phi from the evaluator; and on rigid waters, the extra point
# of Amber and the linear site of ParmEd's topology of GROMACS are one place
# (the same energy). ParmEd cuts and converts the topology.
# Inputs/python_frame_sites.py says what each scenario checks.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber CPU Double %t/amber-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=AMBER,AMBERDOUBLE -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: env MDIR_SITE_SPREAD=derived %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber CPU Double %t/amber-Double-derived | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=AMBER,AMBERDOUBLE -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber CPU Mixed %t/amber-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=AMBER,AMBERMIXED -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide placement CPU Double %t/placement-Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PLACEMENT -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide placement CPU Mixed %t/placement-Mixed | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=PLACEMENT -DMODE="CPU Mixed"

# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles), 2 frames: the product in theta against central differences of the NumPy Phi
# AMBERDOUBLE: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the same against central differences of the rows along the cotangent
# AMBERMIXED: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the product in theta in mixed precision against that in double
# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the product in theta with another cotangent on the sites
# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the derivative in the positions with another cotangent on the sites
# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the derivative in the positions of the part of the extra points against a complex step of the NumPy Phi
# AMBER: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the same against Richardson differences of the NumPy Phi (h = 4e-06)
# AMBERDOUBLE: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the derivative in the positions against Richardson differences of Phi from the evaluator (h = 4e-06)
# AMBERMIXED: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the derivative in the positions in mixed precision against that in double
# AMBER: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters, 182 particles): the product in theta of the variant equals D381's, to the bit; the rows of the sites are zero
# PLACEMENT: [[MODE]]: OPC from Amber and from GROMACS (40 waters, a = {{[0-9.]+}}), 2 frames of rigid waters: the energy, through the places of the sites
